The Second River understood now. They weren't enemies. They weren't even failed partners. They were two consciousness trapped in a system designed to make cooperation impossible, each living their own honest experience of betrayal.

"I see you now," the Second River said. "Not as betrayer. As fellow victim of fog so thick it made phantoms of us both."

Zero met zero. Not in hostility.

In recognition.
